Notes
-----
* SonarQube already runs on SQ1. http://localhost:9000 on SC1 reaches it.
  First login: admin / admin, then set a throwaway password.
* The application is an API without HTML pages to crawl, so ZAP's spider
  finds next to nothing on its own. Import the OpenAPI definition above into
  ZAP (Import -> Import an OpenAPI Definition from a URL), then run the
  Active Scan against http://sc1:{{ cr13_app_port }}.
* ZAP runs on another machine, so it cannot reach 127.0.0.1 on SC1. The
  application still binds to 127.0.0.1 only. SC1 forwards port {{ cr13_app_port }} on
  {{ cr13_ip_sc1 }} to it, and the Windows firewall admits that port from OWZ1
  ({{ cr13_ip_owz1 }}) and nothing else. Do not change the bind address.
* If a command is "not recognized" although verify-cr-env.ps1 says OK, the
  window is older than the installation: run fix-path.ps1 or sign out and in.
* To look at the containers:  ssh {{ cr13_trainee_user }}@sq1   or   ssh {{ cr13_trainee_user }}@owz1
  then:  cd /opt/cr13 && docker compose ps

